\newlabel{fig:sch-cb-pnp}{{4}{8}{Common-base circuits for the PNP transistor: (a) input-characteristic circuit, $|V_{CC}| = \SI {5}{\volt }$, $R_E = \SI {1}{\kilo \ohm }$, $V_{EE}$ swept; (b) output-characteristic circuit, $V_{EE} = \SI {0}{\volt }$ (stepped to \SI {5}{\volt }), $R_C = \SI {100}{\ohm }$, $V_{CC}$ swept. The source polarities and the current directions are reversed with respect to Figure~\ref {fig:sch-cb-npn}}{figure.caption.6}{}}
